Package: PbStatR
Type: Package
Title: Student-Friendly Plant Breeding Statistical Analysis Toolkit
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: 
    person("First", "Last", email = "you@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A comprehensive, beginner-friendly toolkit for plant breeding and
    quantitative genetics. Provides a one-call guided analysis (pb_analyze) plus
    genetic variability parameters (GCV, PCV, ECV, heritability, genetic
    advance), ANOVA with post-hoc mean comparisons (Tukey, Duncan, LSD, SNK,
    Scheffe) and assumption diagnostics, correlation and path analysis,
    multivariate analysis and diversity via 'FactoMineR' and 'factoextra' (PCA,
    HCPC, clustering) with publication-ready 'ggplot2' heatmaps and figures,
    experimental design layout through 'agricolae' and field maps through
    'FielDHub' (CRD, RCBD, LSD, factorial, split-plot, alpha-lattice,
    augmented), multi-environment trials, stability analysis (AMMI, WAASB,
    Eberhart-Russell), biometrical genetics (line x tester, Griffing diallel,
    generation mean analysis), mixed linear models with BLUP via 'lme4',
    genomic selection (GRM, GBLUP, cross-validation), GWAS, QTL mapping,
    molecular diversity, envirotyping, Bayesian analysis, and breeding pipeline
    simulation via 'AlphaSimR'.
